    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. it's just weird because it seems so random. like, is there any way to tell if it's just a simple fix or if it's something more annoying? i'm worried i'm gonna be chasing some weird phantom issue that doesn't actually make sense",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the noise only happens under load—meaning when you step on the gas and the engine is working hard—it strongly suggests a slip, which points to the belt or its tension. If the noise is constant, even when idling, it might indicate a failing pulley bearing or an issue with the tensioner itself. A simple replacement of the serpentine belt is often the fix, which is usually a straightforward job, but if the tensioner or a pulley is damaged, that adds a bit more complexity. You'll want a mechanic to take a look to confirm, but don't panic; it's rarely a \"phantom issue.\"",
      "source": "target",
